Package: pulseR
Title: Probabilistic Hierarchical Spatial Regionalization
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jonathan", "Jupke", , "jonjup@duck.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6815-1855"))
Description: Builds three-level hierarchical regionalizations of spatial
    units with uncertainty at every level, following the PULSE framework
    (Probabilistic Unified Landscape Stratification Engine). Level 1 forms
    contiguous regions from an ensemble of randomly cut minimum spanning
    trees, extending the SKATER algorithm (Assuncao et al. 2006)
    <doi:>, and summarises the ensemble with
    'salso' (Dahl et al. 2022) <doi:10.1080/10618600.2022.2069779>.
    Level 2 fits Gaussian mixture models with 'mclust' within each region.
    Level 3 groups units by the composition of types in their
    neighbourhood. Each level returns crisp labels and membership
    probabilities, and diagnostics report ensemble convergence and
    stability.
